\pard\b\f0\fs28 DetectIt - Hardware Detector\par
\par
\b0\fs20 A professional Windows application for detecting and displaying detailed hardware information about your computer.\par
\par
\b Features:\par
\b0\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\bullet}}\f0 Comprehensive CPU information (name, cores, speed, architecture)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Detailed memory modules (capacity, speed, manufacturer)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Motherboard specifications (manufacturer, model, serial)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}GPU information (name, VRAM, resolution, refresh rate)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Storage drives (model, size, interface type)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Network adapters (name, MAC address, speed)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Operating system details and configuration\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Export hardware information to text file\par
\par
\b System Requirements:\par
\b0\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit)\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}No additional software required\par
{\pntext\f1\bullet\tab}Administrator privileges recommended for full hardware access\par
\par
\b Installation:\par
\b0\par
1. Run DetectIt_Setup_v1.0.0.exe\par
2. Follow the installation wizard\par
3. Choose installation directory (default: C:\\Program Files\\DetectIt)\par
4. Select Start Menu folder\par
5. Optionally create desktop shortcut\par
6. Complete installation\par
\par
\b Usage:\par
\b0\par
1. Launch DetectIt from Start Menu or Desktop shortcut\par
2. View hardware information organized by category in the tree view\par
3. Click on any category or item to see detailed information\par
4. Use the Refresh button to rescan hardware\par
5. Use the Export button to save information to a text file\par
\par
\b Note:\par
\b0 For complete hardware information, run DetectIt as Administrator.\par
\par
\b Support:\par
\b0 For issues or questions, visit: https://github.com/detectit\par
\par
